1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:06,020
When you buy a used car for 30,000 złoty, you take it to a diagnostic station:

2
00:00:06,020 --> 00:00:10,980
you measure the paint thickness, check the frame geometry and look for oil leaks.

3
00:00:10,980 --> 00:00:14,380
When you buy a house or a plot for 1,000,000 złoty…

4
00:00:14,380 --> 00:00:18,880
you look at nice photos on Otodom and take the developer's word for it!

5
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:22,220
Nobody does a technical X-ray of the land!

6
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:26,880
We built one from satellite data: Poznań Trend Detective.

7
00:00:27,150 --> 00:00:31,950
Type an address or draw an area, and you get a technical inspection of the land:

8
00:00:31,950 --> 00:00:36,990
building history and forecast, a building-risk score, trees cut, heat,

9
00:00:36,990 --> 00:00:42,690
groundwater-flood areas (PIG-PIB), terrain hollows, radar and the price per square metre.

10
00:00:43,020 --> 00:00:47,340
Around Poznań, built-up land more than doubled in 30 years.

11
00:00:47,340 --> 00:00:50,140
The model shows where the city grows next.

12
00:00:50,140 --> 00:00:54,940
Tested on years it never saw, it found 56% of new building.

13
00:00:54,940 --> 00:00:57,360
A ranking, not a verdict.

14
00:00:57,460 --> 00:01:02,900
Summer nights warmed significantly almost everywhere, and not one square cooled.

15
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:07,790
And the faster a municipality grew, the faster its summer days warmed.

16
00:01:07,790 --> 00:01:17,470
Data: NASA MODIS, NISAR, Landsat, Sentinel-1, Copernicus DEM, GUS and IMGW.

17
00:01:17,470 --> 00:01:21,650
Every trend is tested with Mann-Kendall and Theil-Sen.

18
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:26,340
Poznań Trend Detective. Check the land before you sign.
